A||||8||VAROOM||Bad Coil ??||||5||
Z||000000||VAROOM||02-28-2000||02:49 PM||||Hey out there. The GT runs good, but still have a small problem. If the car is cold, it starts right up. If you drive for a long distance then shut it off it will start if it has been less than a few minutes. But if it sits for a longer time, it will turn over, almost start, but will not run. Then you have to wait till it almost is cold again before it will run. Then it's ok till the next time. Need some feedback .Thanx.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||02-28-2000||03:07 PM||||I would start with the electronic module , they do act the way you describe.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||02-28-2000||04:03 PM||||I bet it's the pickup coil in the distributor.  If the coil goes(the one with the spark plug lookin wire going to the middle of the distributor cap)Those USUALLY stay dead. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||RICK||02-28-2000||06:39 PM||||If you have a Haynes manual they describe how to test the coil and pick-up coil.  You can pull the ig module and take it to Napa, Auto-Zone, whoever and they can test that for you.<BR>I was having a problem like that, sometimes it would start, sometimes it wouldn't, I pulled a plug wire and I wouldn't get a spark to ground from it.  It ended up being the ig module||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||02-28-2000||08:00 PM||||mine does the same...   put a new coil on it and same results... so i may try the pickup coil, hope that is it.||||reg||3
Z||000005||wwh0001||03-01-2000||09:33 AM||||Your problem may be the ignition system, but it sounds more like a fuel related problem. You are having a heat soke issue. Your injectors are probably leaking, creating a flooding condition when you car sits for more than a few minutes. If it sits for a longer period of time the fuel rail has time release the pressure. simple test. After it sits for a couple of minutes( time frame when it won't start) press the gas pedal to the floor to start, it it starts, then you know your problem is leaking injectors causing a flooding condition.||||reg||1
Z||000006||chris6878||03-01-2000||01:06 PM||||your good...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>thats exactly what i have to do to get mine to start after it gets warm and sets a while... <P>what would one need to do...   get new seals for the injectors (i think there are 2 seals on each injector right?)<P>thanks<BR>chris||||reg||3
Z||000007||Carrolles||03-02-2000||01:06 PM||||Each injector has an o-ring on each end.  They are the same size.  Pontiac wanted around $25 for the set of 12.  I paid 50 cents each for them at Pep Boys.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||03-02-2000||01:11 PM||||Wow. You mean I can just replace the seals?! I have always thought my injectors were leaking(only slightly)but was under the impression I would have to buy all new injectors. Cool. Maybe next time I have the intake off, I'll do them.||||reg||1
